---
import Footer from '../components/landing/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/landing.css';

const title = 'Compare approaches | TeamCTL';
const description = 'Choose how you want your agents to work together. TeamCTL combines configurable roles and structures, background sessions and an agent mailbox.';
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://teamctl.run/compare/" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="16x16 32x32 48x48" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" sizes="any" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="TeamCTL" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://teamctl.run/compare/" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://teamctl.run/brand/social-cover.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="TeamCTL — Create autonomous teams of agents." />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://teamctl.run/brand/social-cover.png" />
  </head>
  <body class="landing">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-nav">
      <a class="brand-link" href="/" aria-label="TeamCTL home"><img src="/brand/teamctl-head.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />TeamCTL</a>
      <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/getting-started/">Docs</a><a class="nav-github" href="https://github.com/Alireza29675/teamctl">GitHub ↗</a></nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main" class="compare page-width">
      <header class="compare-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Choosing your setup</p>
        <h1>How do you want your agents to work together?</h1>
        <p class="compare-lede">TeamCTL is a platform for defining the team itself: its roles, structure and conversations. Other tools approach agent work through session management, orchestration frameworks or messaging.</p>
      </header>

      <section class="compare-section" aria-labelledby="teamctl-heading">
        <h2 id="teamctl-heading">Choose TeamCTL when you want to define and run a team.</h2>
        <p>Create peer research partners, a project team or an organization with separate project rosters. Write the roles and relationships, choose the runtimes, and share the configuration others need to reproduce the setup.</p>
        <div class="scope-grid">
          <article><h3>Your structure</h3><p>Markdown roles and YAML configuration define who does what, who reports to whom and which channels connect them.</p><a href="/reference/team-compose-yaml/">Configuration reference ↗</a></article>
          <article><h3>Background sessions</h3><p>Real Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode or Gemini CLI sessions run in tmux while the host and provider access remain available.</p><a href="/concepts/runtimes/">Runtime support ↗</a></article>
          <article><h3>Connected conversations</h3><p>A SQLite-backed MCP mailbox carries messages between agents. The terminal UI lets you inspect sessions and conversations.</p><a href="/concepts/channels/">Channels and messages ↗</a></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="compare-section" aria-labelledby="approaches-heading">
        <h2 id="approaches-heading">Explore the neighboring approaches.</h2>
        <p>These are summaries of each project’s stated focus, checked on October 10, 2026. Follow the upstream documentation for current features, requirements and limits.</p>
        <div class="approaches">
          <article><span class="shape-number">SESSION MANAGEMENT</span><h3><a href="https://github.com/smtg-ai/claude-squad">Claude Squad ↗</a></h3><p>A terminal app for managing multiple coding-agent sessions in separate workspaces, with task navigation and change review.</p></article>
          <article><span class="shape-number">AGENT HARNESS</span><h3><a href="https://github.com/ruvnet/ruflo">Ruflo / formerly Claude Flow ↗</a></h3><p>An agent harness with orchestration, memory and MCP tooling for agent workflows. Its setup and capabilities are documented in the upstream repository.</p></article>
          <article><span class="shape-number">COORDINATION LAYER</span><h3><a href="https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/mcp_agent_mail_rust">MCP Agent Mail (Rust) ↗</a></h3><p>A messaging and coordination layer with agent identities, inboxes, searchable threads and advisory file leases.</p></article>
          <article><span class="shape-number">YOUR OWN TOOLING</span><h3><a href="https://github.com/tmux/tmux">tmux + scripts ↗</a></h3><p>Use a terminal multiplexer and scripts to create a workflow around your own sessions, configuration and communication tools.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="compare-section" aria-labelledby="boundaries-heading">
        <h2 id="boundaries-heading">What to expect from TeamCTL today.</h2>
        <p>Closing the terminal UI leaves agent sessions running. Rebooting the host stops live processes. System-native supervision through systemd or launchd is planned.</p>
        <p>Each agent keeps its own session and conversation history. Messages connect agents; they do not merge their context. Agent instructions and runtime permissions define action boundaries.</p>
        <p>Configure Telegram for conversations and explicit approval requests. TeamCTL’s mailbox is not a universal action gate or a sandbox.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/getting-started/">Set up your first team</a>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .compare { max-width: 66rem; }
  .compare-header { padding-block: 5rem 4rem; }
  .compare-header h1 { max-width: 17ch; font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 4.4rem); }
  .compare-lede { max-width: 43rem; color: var(--fg-mute); margin-top: 1.75rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .compare-section { padding-block: 3.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .compare-section h2 { max-width: 28ch; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.4rem); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .compare-section > p { max-width: 48rem; color: var(--fg-mute); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .scope-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 2.5rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .scope-grid h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .scope-grid p { margin-block: 1rem; color: var(--fg-mute); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .scope-grid a { font-size: 0.8rem; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; }
  .approaches { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 3rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .approaches h3 { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 1.3rem; }
  .approaches h3 a { text-decoration: none; }
  .approaches p { color: var(--fg-mute); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .scope-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } }
  @media (max-width: 540px) { .compare-header { padding-block: 3rem; } .approaches { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; } }
</style>
